# Crow Governance

Before any implementation work:

1. Read [`docs/crow/START-HERE.md`](../../docs/crow/START-HERE.md) and [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)
2. Read [`docs/crow/CURRENT-STATE.md`](../../docs/crow/CURRENT-STATE.md) for verified implementation truth
3. Verify repository path, current branch, HEAD, and working-tree state
4. Identify the active milestone scope, in-scope items, out-of-scope items, and protected boundaries

## Authority boundaries (non-negotiable)

- Payment status must never grant or modify authoritative roles or tenant membership
- SAREA adapts presentation only — it never grants permission
- CroAI is advisory by default — it must not bypass CyberCrow or grant authority
- Account verification (email, phone) proves account control only — not tenant membership or ProCrow access
- Request submission does not create a tenant; Discovery does not grant authority
- Blueprint approval must precede tenant build

## Prohibited without explicit owner authorization

- Production deployment or promotion
- Pushing to `main` or merging draft PRs
- Hosted database migrations outside the controlled-migration workflow
- Hosted business-data writes
- Creating duplicate canonical definitions in code or docs

## Required practices

- Link to the authoritative owner document instead of redefining concepts
- Distinguish product direction from current implementation state
- Record design–implementation gaps in [`docs/crow/GAP-LEDGER.md`](../../docs/crow/GAP-LEDGER.md)
- Run repository validation gates (typecheck, lint, build) before claiming completion
- Never claim owner acceptance — deployed evidence and explicit owner review are required
- Stop on authority conflicts and report rather than silently resolving

## Milestone discipline

Use [`docs/crow/milestones/MILESTONE-TEMPLATE.md`](../../docs/crow/milestones/MILESTONE-TEMPLATE.md). One domain per milestone when possible. Update current-state and gap ledger as durable outputs.
